      "text": "I understand the worry at the moment I'd say it's an inflammatory arthritis flare, and we'll know more once the X-rays of the hands is back let's get X-rays of the hands, for inflammatory arthritis. Blood tests is what I'd like next, for inflammatory arthritis the result will help us decide whether anything more is needed the treatment will be methotrexate, 10 milligrams, once a week, long term that's for inflammatory arthritis"
